# /etc/compose-drift-guard.env — config for compose-drift-guard.sh (0600 root)
#
# Create a "Push" monitor in Uptime Kuma (uptime.owner.example) named
# "agent-box compose drift" and paste its push URL here. Until set, the guard runs
# and journals but cannot alert.
#
# THE INTERVAL RULE (ORB-154, do not skip this). Heartbeat interval AND retry
# interval must both be at least twice compose-drift-guard.timer's period. The timer
# is hourly, so both are 10800s — three times over, deliberately.
#
# The line that used to be here said "heartbeat interval 3600s, retries 2", and that
# instruction is what broke this monitor. A 3600s window against a pusher that fires
# every 3610s (systemd's OnUnitActiveSec measures from the END of the last run, so it
# drifts) means Kuma calls "No heartbeat in the time window" seconds before each push
# arrives. At one point the window was 1200s against the same hourly pusher and it was
# worse: a red and a green in Slack EVERY HOUR from 4 to 19 August, 279 false downs.
# That is how a real alert becomes invisible — which is exactly what happened when the
# nightly backup failed three nights running and nobody noticed (ORB-150).
#
# ALSO SET maxretries=3. Drift is normal for a while after every deploy: the repo moves
# when you push, the box moves when you deploy, and the baseline only re-aligns when
# someone runs `compose-drift-guard.sh --accept`. Four consecutive hourly down pushes
# (~4h) before Kuma notifies keeps an ordinary deploy quiet while still surfacing real,
# persistent drift the same day.
KUMA_PUSH_URL=

# Optional overrides (defaults shown):
# STATE_DIR=/opt/agent-box/drift-guard
# REPO_DIR=/opt/agent-box/drift-guard/overlay
# REPO_COMPOSE=$REPO_DIR/box/compose.yaml
# REPO_OVERRIDE=$REPO_DIR/box/compose.override.yaml
# BOX_DIR=/opt/agent-box
# DEPLOY_KEY=/root/.ssh/overlay_deploy_ro
